# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the two values from the Supabase
# dashboard's Connect dialog. `.env.local` is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# The VITE_ prefix is not decoration. Vite only exposes variables starting with
# VITE_ to browser code; anything else is simply absent at runtime. Copying the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ names that Supabase's Connect dialog shows by default leaves both
# values `undefined` with no build error and no console warning — the app just
# fails to reach the database.
#
# Both values below are safe in the browser bundle and safe to commit to a
# private repo. They are not passwords. What actually protects a student's data
# is row level security in the database, which is why the anon key being public
# by design is fine. Never put the database password or a `service_role` /
# `sb_secret_` key in here: those bypass every policy.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-OR-PUBLISHABLE-KEY
